# Four-ply info spelling: April 2006 UCI specification, info and Move format
# https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/#engine-info and fisher-8hc question 1
# (order of fields approved by the owner 2026-11-24; these sessions staged
# 2026-11-24 and awaiting the owner's approval). D3–D6 supply the
# allowances for the principal variation, time and nodes per second. The fisher-2aj.2 sources and
# comments below supply the retained scores, node counts and reply order.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# and fisher-l7f owner decisions from 2026-11-22.
# Search: fisher-2aj rules 1 to 7, 9 and 10. Exact search values
# were checked by exhaustive enumeration with python-chess 1.11.2.
# Starting score: four-ply minimax with python-chess 1.11.2 followed rules
# 1 to 7. An independent reviewer reproduced cp 0 and per-ply counts
# 20/400/8902/197281 with their own minimax. See expectations/perft.epd.
# Searched transcript written 2026-11-23.
> position startpos
> go infinite
# Rule 9 sends info before the reply to isready. The move waits for stop.
# Rules 1 to 7 and 10. Published perft counts sum to 206603. See the header for cp 0.
< info depth 4 score cp 0 time {time} nodes 206603 nps {nps} pv {pv}
> isready
# UCI go infinite and isready. No bestmove precedes readyok.
< readyok
# The owner's decision discards the held move on UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
